1
00:00:03,095 --> 00:00:03,957
Look, up there,

2
00:00:04,007 --> 00:00:06,571
green curtains are dancing without a sound!

3
00:00:06,621 --> 00:00:07,787
But why does the sky

4
00:00:07,837 --> 00:00:09,296
light up near the poles?

5
00:00:10,060 --> 00:00:13,712
Mila takes out her compass, and the needle points north,

6
00:00:13,762 --> 00:00:15,431
right where the sky glows…

7
00:00:15,481 --> 00:00:17,597
A clue: Earth is a giant magnet!

8
00:00:18,362 --> 00:00:19,876
Discovery mission!

9
00:00:22,392 --> 00:00:22,979
Mini mode!

10
00:00:23,029 --> 00:00:25,020
The Sun doesn't only give light:

11
00:00:25,070 --> 00:00:29,228
it constantly blows billions of tiny electric specks toward Earth.

12
00:00:29,278 --> 00:00:30,681
That's the solar wind.

13
00:00:31,478 --> 00:00:33,067
Luckily, Earth is a giant magnet:

14
00:00:33,117 --> 00:00:34,756
its magnetic field forms a shield.

15
00:00:34,806 --> 00:00:36,346
That shield deflects the specks…

16
00:00:36,396 --> 00:00:38,581
and guides some of them toward the two poles,

17
00:00:38,631 --> 00:00:39,824
sliding along its lines.

18
00:00:40,645 --> 00:00:43,057
Way up high, a hundred kilometers up,

19
00:00:43,107 --> 00:00:44,587
the specks hit the air.

20
00:00:44,637 --> 00:00:47,647
So oxygen glows green, nitrogen blue and pink,

21
00:00:47,697 --> 00:00:48,778
like a neon sign…

22
00:00:48,828 --> 00:00:50,026
that's the aurora!

23
00:00:50,818 --> 00:00:52,843
Auroras form a ring around both poles:

24
00:00:52,893 --> 00:00:56,065
northern lights in the north, southern lights in the south.

25
00:00:56,115 --> 00:00:58,522
And when the Sun blows hard, the ring widens…

26
00:00:58,572 --> 00:00:59,937
we see them farther away!

27
00:01:00,710 --> 00:01:01,909
And that's why the sky

28
00:01:01,959 --> 00:01:03,378
lights up near the poles.

29
00:01:04,211 --> 00:01:07,704
Specks from the Sun, guided to the poles by Earth's magnet,

30
00:01:07,754 --> 00:01:09,556
make the air glow way up high.

31
00:01:10,728 --> 00:01:13,297
With an adult: bring a magnet near a compass…

32
00:01:13,347 --> 00:01:14,519
and the needle turns!

33
00:01:14,569 --> 00:01:15,684
It feels the magnet,

34
00:01:15,734 --> 00:01:17,305
just as it feels the Earth.

35
00:01:18,211 --> 00:01:20,253
And why does rain have a smell?

36
00:01:20,303 --> 00:01:21,653
The answer tomorrow.
